body:
The API can merge construction elements, list what an element is merged with, and remove a merge
between two elements. Tapir exposes none of this. That makes it impossible to automate cleaning up
the junctions of slabs, beams and similar elements, or to check them.

Please add:
- **`MergeElements`:**
  - **Input:** `elements: [{elementId}]`, which are merged together.
  - **Result:** one `ExecutionResult`.
  - **Undo:** undoable, because `APIERR_NEEDSUNDOSCOPE` shows it needs an undo scope.
- **`GetMergedElements`:**
  - **Input:** `elements`.
  - **Output per element:** `mergedElements: [{elementId}]`, or an error.
- **`UnmergeElements`:**
  - **Input:** `[{elementId1, elementId2}]`.
  - **Result:** an `executionResults` entry per pair. Undoable.

API (identical in AC25–AC30, `ACAPinc.h`):
```cpp
__APIEXPORT GSErrCode ACAPI_Element_Merge_Elements (const GS::Array<API_Guid>& guid_ElementsToMerge);
// NoError; APIERR_NEEDSUNDOSCOPE; APIERR_BADDATABASE, APIERR_NOTMINE - cannot operate on the current database;
// APIERR_BADINDEX - invalid IDs; APIERR_BADPARS; APIERR_BADELEMENTTYPE - "not construction element type".

__APIEXPORT GSErrCode ACAPI_Element_Merge_GetMergedElements (const API_Guid& guid_Element, GS::Array<API_Guid>* guid_MergedElements);
// "gets elements are merged with the given element." Same errors without NEEDSUNDOSCOPE.

__APIEXPORT GSErrCode ACAPI_Element_Merge_Remove (const API_Guid& guid_Element1, const API_Guid& guid_Element2);
// "removes merge connection between the elements." NEEDSUNDOSCOPE, BADDATABASE/NOTMINE, BADINDEX, BADELEMENTTYPE.
```
The DevKit gives no list of supported types beyond "construction element", so report each error as
it comes and don't pre-filter. In the PR, ask the tester to check which element types merge.

Archicad elements can carry a web link: a URL with a description. Tapir can neither read nor set it.
Links to product data sheets, BIM object pages or issue trackers are a common scripted task.

Please add:
- **`GetURLReferencesOfElements`:**
  - **Input:** `elements`.
  - **Output per element:** `{url, description}`, `null` when the element has none
    (`APIERR_NOUSERDATA`), or an error.
- **`SetURLReferencesOfElements`:**
  - **Input:** `[{elementId, url, description}]`.
  - **Result:** an `executionResults` entry per element.

API (AC27+ names; `ACAPI_Database.h`; struct in `APIdefs_Database.h`):
```cpp
struct API_ElemURLRef {
	char urlLink [512];      // "The URL link (e.g., "http://www.graphisoft.com")"
	char description [256];  // "Description for the URL above (e.g., "GRAPHISOFT Home Page")."
};
__APIEXPORT GSErrCode ACAPI_Element_GetElementURLRef (API_Elem_Head* elem_Head, API_ElemURLRef* elemURLRef);
// NoError; APIERR_BADPARS; APIERR_BADINDEX - not in the database; APIERR_BADID - "The element cannot hold a URL reference";
// APIERR_DELETED; APIERR_NOUSERDATA - "The element does not hold a URL reference."
__APIEXPORT GSErrCode ACAPI_Element_SetElementURLRef (API_Elem_Head* elemHead, API_ElemURLRef* elemURLRef);
// Same, plus APIERR_MOREUSER - "The element already holds a URL reference."
// Remarks: "The same group of elements can hold a URL reference as user data."
```
AC25/AC26: `ACAPI_Database (APIDb_GetElementURLRefID / APIDb_SetElementURLRefID, (void*) &elemHead, &urlRef)`
(`APIdefs_Database.h`: "par1: API_Elem_Head* par2: API_ElemURLRef*").

Notes:
- **Text encoding:** both fields are fixed-size `char` arrays. Convert from UTF-8 with `CH_UTF8` and
  reject texts that don't fit (511/255 bytes), instead of truncating them.
- **Replacing an existing link:** `APIERR_MOREUSER` means a second Set on an element that already has a
  link fails. The DevKit has no separate delete call for it. Report that error as is, and ask the tester
  to check in Archicad whether a link can be replaced. Change the behaviour only once that's known.

Every Archicad construction element has category values: **Structural Function** (Load-Bearing / Non-Load-Bearing / Undefined), **Position** (Exterior / Interior / Undefined) and **Renovation Status** (Existing / To Be Demolished / New). They drive IFC export (`LoadBearing`, `IsExternal`), schedules and renovation filters, so setting them in bulk is a common scripted task.

Tapir can neither read nor set them. The API calls are already in `MigrationHelper.hpp` (`TAPIR_Element_SetCategoryValue`), but they are only used when applying a Favorite (`FavoritesCommands.cpp`).

Please add, in the Element group:
- **`GetElementCategories`:**
  - **Input:** none.
  - **Output:** every category with `categoryId` (`{guid}`), its `type` (`StructuralFunction`, `Position`, `RenovationStatus`, `RenovationFilter`, `BRI`), its localized `name`, and its values, each with `categoryValueId` (`{guid}`), `name`, `isVisibleOnUI` and `usableAsCriteria`.
- **`GetCategoryValuesOfElements`:**
  - **Input:** `elements`, plus optional `categories`: a list of `type` values; omitted means all.
  - **Output per element:** a list of `{type, categoryId, categoryValueId, name}`, or an error.
- **`SetCategoryValuesOfElements`:**
  - **Input:** `[{elementId, type, categoryValueId}]`.
  - **Result:** an `executionResults` entry per element.
  - Look the value up by guid in the category's value list, and fail with a clear message when it doesn't belong to that category.
  - Run all changes in one `ACAPI_CallUndoableCommand`.

API (AC30 `ACAPI_Database.h` / `ACAPinc.h`; structs in `APIdefs_Elements.h`, identical in AC25–30):
```cpp
typedef enum {
	API_ElemCategory_Undefined = 0,
	API_ElemCategory_StructuralFunction,
	API_ElemCategory_Position,
	API_ElemCategory_RenovationStatus,
	API_ElemCategory_RenovationFilter,
	API_ElemCategory_BRI            // "(available only in GER localized version)"
} API_ElemCategoryID;

struct API_ElemCategory {
	API_Guid            guid;
	API_ElemCategoryID  categoryID;
	GS::uchar_t         name[API_UniLongNameLen];   // "Localized name of the category."
	bool                filler_1[2];
};

struct API_ElemCategoryValue {
	API_Guid            guid;
	API_ElemCategory    category;
	GS::uchar_t         name[API_UniLongNameLen];
	bool                isVisibleOnUI;
	bool                usableAsCriteria;
};

// AC27+
GSErrCode ACAPI_Category_GetElementCategories (GS::Array<API_ElemCategory>* categoryList);
GSErrCode ACAPI_Category_GetElementCategoryValues (const API_ElemCategory* category, GS::Array<API_ElemCategoryValue>* categoryValueList);
	// "The category identified by guid or categoryID."  APIERR_BADID - "Incorrect category was specified (bad guid and categoryID)."
GSErrCode ACAPI_Category_GetCategoryValue (const API_Guid& elemGuid, const API_ElemCategory& elemCategory, API_ElemCategoryValue* elemCategoryValue);
GSErrCode ACAPI_Category_SetCategoryValue (const API_Guid& elemGuid, const API_ElemCategory& elemCategory, const API_ElemCategoryValue& elemCategoryValue);
	// APIERR_BADPARS - "elemCategoryValue or elemCategory is incorrect."  APIERR_BADID - "Incorrect elemGuid was specified."
	// "To get the list of category values in a given category use ACAPI_Category_GetElementCategoryValues."
```

AC25/AC26:
- **Get and Set on an element:** `ACAPI_Element_GetCategoryValue` / `ACAPI_Element_SetCategoryValue`, with the same parameters.
- **The category and value lists:** `ACAPI_Database (APIDb_GetElementCategoriesID, GS::Array<API_ElemCategory>*)` and `ACAPI_Database (APIDb_GetElementCategoryValuesID, const API_ElemCategory*, GS::Array<API_ElemCategoryValue>*)`.

Add `TAPIR_` wrappers for the three new calls next to `TAPIR_Element_SetCategoryValue` in `MigrationHelper.hpp`.

Notes:
- **Names are localized,** so scripts must use the `type` enum and the value guids, never names. Say so in the descriptions.
- **Renovation Status** is also on the element header. Check in Archicad that setting it through the category changes what the Renovation palette shows, and say on the pull request what was found.
- **Elements without categories:** element types without categories (annotations, for example) should get a per-element error, not fail the whole call.
- Add `Examples/element_categories.py`: list the categories, set a few walls to Load-Bearing and Exterior, and read them back.

Composite walls, slabs and roofs, complex profiles and other multi-material elements consist of **components**, one per building material skin or profile part. Archicad schedules list them (component listing), and they have their own property values: building material, the component's thickness, area and volume, and custom properties of the building material.

Tapir reads properties of whole elements only (`GetPropertyValuesOfElements`). A script cannot get a per-material breakdown, for example "m³ of concrete and m² of insulation in these walls". Tapir doesn't call any of the component APIs below.

Please add, in the Property group:
- **`GetComponentsOfElements`:**
  - **Input:** `elements`.
  - **Output per element:** a list of `componentId` values (`{guid}`), or an error.
- **`GetPropertyValuesOfElementComponents`:**
  - **Input:** `[{elementId, componentId}]` and `properties` (property ids, as in `GetPropertyValuesOfElements`).
  - **Output:** per component, the property values in the same shape as `GetPropertyValuesOfElements`, so clients can reuse its parsing.
  - Reuse the existing property value conversion.
- Optionally, **`GetPropertyDefinitionsOfElementComponents`**, which returns the property ids available on a component, through the filter overload below.

API (AC27+ names, AC30 `ACAPinc.h`; structs in `APIdefs_Component.h`, the same in AC25–30):
```cpp
struct API_ComponentID {
	API_Guid componentGuid;
};
struct API_ElemComponentID {
	API_Guid        elemGuid;
	API_ComponentID componentID;
};

GSErrCode ACAPI_Element_GetComponents (const API_Guid& elemGuid, GS::Array<API_ElemComponentID>& elemComponents);
	// "Retrieves the components of an element."  APIERR_BADID - "The elemGuid did not refer to a valid element."

GSErrCode ACAPI_Element_GetPropertyDefinitions (const API_ElemComponentID& elemComponent, API_PropertyDefinitionFilter filter, GS::Array<API_PropertyDefinition>& propertyDefinitions);
GSErrCode ACAPI_Element_GetPropertyValue (const API_ElemComponentID& elemComponent, const API_Guid& propertyDefinitionGuid, API_Property& property);
GSErrCode ACAPI_Element_GetPropertyValues (const API_ElemComponentID& elemComponent, const GS::Array<API_PropertyDefinition>& propertyDefinitions, GS::Array<API_Property>& properties);
GSErrCode ACAPI_Element_GetPropertyValuesByGuid (const API_ElemComponentID& elemComponent, const GS::Array<API_Guid>& propertyDefinitions, GS::Array<API_Property>& properties);
```
AC25/AC26: `ACAPI_Element_GetComponents` has the same name; the four property calls are named
`ACAPI_ElemComponent_GetPropertyDefinitions`, `ACAPI_ElemComponent_GetPropertyValue`,
`ACAPI_ElemComponent_GetPropertyValues` and `ACAPI_ElemComponent_GetPropertyValuesByGuid`, with the same parameters
(AC25 `ACAPinc.h`). Add `TAPIR_` wrappers in `MigrationHelper.hpp`.

Notes:
- **Not `ACAPI_Element_GetComponents_Obsolete`.** It takes an `API_Elem_Head*` and is a different, older call. Use the `API_Guid` overload above.
- **The component guid alone does not identify a component.** It is only meaningful together with its element, so the output and the property input always carry both ids.
- **Reading only.** Component property values come from the building material and the geometry. This issue doesn't write them.
- Add `Examples/element_components.py`: for the walls of the test project, list components with their building material name and component volume, and sum the volume per building material.
- Say in the description which element types return components, after checking in Archicad (composite and profiled walls, slabs, roofs, shells, beams and columns, at least).

The scale of the current floor plan, section, elevation, detail or worksheet window (the 1:100 in the bottom bar) cannot be read or changed by a script unless the window is a saved view:
- `GetViewSettings` / `SetViewSettings` read and write `drawingScale` of a **saved view**;
- the scale of the window that is open right now has no command.

Scripts that switch between plan scales, or need the scale for anything drawn in paper units (text size, line spacing, symbol size, a Drawing's placement), have to guess it.

Please add, in the Application group next to `GetCurrentWindowType`:
- **`GetCurrentWindowDrawingScale`:**
  - **Output:** `{scale}`, the scale denominator: 100.0 for 1:100, 20.0 for 1:20.
  - Layouts always return 1.0. Say so in the description.
- **`SetCurrentWindowDrawingScale`:**
  - **Input:** `{scale, rebuild}`. `rebuild` is optional, default `false`, and is passed as the API's `zoom` flag.
  - **Result:** an execution result.
  - Reject values outside the range the API accepts with a clear message instead of `APIERR_BADPARS`, and on layouts. Check the exact bounds in Archicad (the docs say "greater than 1 and smaller than 30000"; is 1:1 allowed?).

API (AC27+, `ACAPI_Database.h`):
```cpp
GSErrCode ACAPI_Drawing_GetDrawingScale (double* scale);
	// "Returns the drawing scale of the current database, as each database may have different scale.
	//  Note: for 1:100 drawings 100.0 is returned, for 1:20 drawings 20.0 is returned etc.
	//  For layouts, the return value is always 1.0."   APIERR_BADPARS - dScale is nullptr
GSErrCode ACAPI_Drawing_ChangeDrawingScale (double* scale, bool zoom = false);
	// "zoom [in] Perform a rebuild command after changing the scale."
	// "This function is used to change the drawing scale of the plan. The scale has to be greater than 1 and smaller than 30000."
	// APIERR_BADPARS - "dScale is nullptr or contains wrong value."
```
AC25/AC26: `ACAPI_Database (APIDb_GetDrawingScaleID, double* scale)` and `ACAPI_Database (APIDb_ChangeDrawingScaleID, double* scale, [bool*] zoom)` (`APIdefs_Database.h`: `'GSCL'`, `'CDRS'`).

Notes:
- **Database or window:** the API works on the current *database*. Check in Archicad that the scale of a section or detail window changes that window, not the floor plan, and state in the descriptions which windows it applies to.
- **Undo:** run the change inside `ACAPI_CallUndoableCommand`, as other setting commands do, unless Archicad refuses it there.
- **Example:** add `Examples/current_window_drawing_scale.py`: read the scale, set 1:50, read it back, restore it.

### API functions

ACAPI_Element_ChangeContent

### What should Tapir let you do?

**Use case**
A title-block text on a master layout has three Autotext lines (address from Project Info). We want to remove the third line and keep the other two Autotexts live. Today we cannot do that by API.

**Test** (Archicad 29 AUT, Tapir 1.7.1, on a layout of a test copy, text deleted afterwards)
1. `CreateTexts` with `"text": "<PROJECTNAME>\n<PROJECTNUMBER>\n<SHORTDATE>"` → the text is live: after `SetProjectInfoField PROJECTNUMBER = "WKL519-T"`, `GetDetailsOfElements` shows `…\rWKL519-T\r18/10/2026` (value restored afterwards).
2. `GetDetailsOfElements` returns only the resolved text, and every run has `"effectProtected": false`:
   ```json
   "text":"Wohnbebauung mit 5 Wohneinheiten\rin Kreuzbergl\rWKL519\r18/10/2026",
   "runs":[{"text":"Wohnbebauung mit 5 Wohneinheiten\r", ..., "effectProtected":false}, ...]
   ```
   So a script cannot tell which parts are Autotext or which key they use.
3. `ModifyTexts` with the resolved text minus the last line:
   ```json
   {"textsWithDetails":[{"elementId":{"guid":"37250ADA-CD90-4B4E-86F7-74AB88F5951A"},"text":"Wohnbebauung mit 5 Wohneinheiten\nin Kreuzbergl\nWKL519"}]}
   → {"error":{"code":-2130312696,"message":"Failed to modify the Text."},"success":false}
   ```
4. Side observation (cause unknown, can be a separate issue): `ModifyTexts` with keys, `"text": "<PROJECTNAME>\n<PROJECTNUMBER>"`, succeeds, but the result is `"Wohnbebauung mit 5 Wohneinheiten\rin Kreuzbergl"`: the `<PROJECTNUMBER>` line is missing. Our project name contains a line break.

**Request**
1. `ACAPI_Element_ChangeContent`, e.g. `ChangeTextContent {"elementId", "from", "range", "content"}`. Per the DevKit it replaces a range and keeps the run styles, so the other Autotext runs stay as they are.
2. In `GetDetailsOfElements` for Text/Label, the unresolved content per run (e.g. `rawText` with `<PROJECTNUMBER>`), so the keys can be read and copied to another title block.

### Declarations from the DevKit (optional)

```cpp
// Inc/ACAPI_Goodies.h (Archicad 25–30), from the DevKit docs
// Change the content of a text or a textual label element.
__APIEXPORT GSErrCode ACAPI_Element_ChangeContent (API_ContentPars* contentPars);

// Returns: NoError; APIERR_BADPARS; APIERR_REFUSEDPAR (not a text or textual label);
// APIERR_PAROVERLAP (range overlaps two or more paragraphs); APIERR_PAROVERFLOW (from runs over the content length); APIERR_MEMFULL.
// Remarks (DevKit): modifies the content of a multistyle text or textual label. The styles of the runs won't be lost.
// The new content piece picks up the style of the character at the 'from' position. The content must not contain
// line end characters and ranges may not overlap paragraphs. Non-undoable data structure modifier
// (the DevKit example wraps it in ACAPI_CallUndoableCommand). API_ContentPars: head, from, range, content, separator handles.
```

