### API functions

ACAPI_Element_GetElementsWithClassification

### What should Tapir let you do?

We want to check models against modelling rules that are tied to classifications (GRAPHISOFT Modellierungsrichtlinien AC29), e.g. every "Wand / tragend / außen" must be a composite wall with the reference line on the core outside; every "Fußbodenaufbau" must be a slab without core. Today a script has to call `GetAllElements` and then `GetClassificationsOfElements` for every element, and filter on the client. The reverse query exists in the API.

Proposed: `GetElementsByClassification {"classificationItemIds": [{"classificationItemId": {"guid": "…"}}]}` → per item `{"elements": [{"elementId": …}]}` or an error (`APIERR_BADID`). The ids would come from the existing classification commands.

### Declarations from the DevKit (optional)

```cpp
// From the DevKit docs (Element group)
// Query elements with the given classification.
__APIEXPORT GSErrCode ACAPI_Element_GetElementsWithClassification (const API_Guid& classificationItemGuid, GS::Array<API_Guid>& elemGuids);
// classificationItemGuid [in]: the identifier of the classification item.
// elemGuids [out]: the identifiers of the elements with the given classification.
// Returns: NoError; APIERR_BADID - classificationItemGuid did not refer to a valid classification item.
```

