### API functions

ACAPI::DesignOptions::DesignOptionManager::GetDesignOptionCombinationSettingsOf
ACAPI::DesignOptions::DesignOptionCombinationViewSettings::GetName
ACAPI::DesignOptions::DesignOptionCombinationViewSettings::GetStatus
ACAPI::DesignOptions::DesignOptionCombinationViewSettings::SetMainModelOnly
ACAPI::DesignOptions::DesignOptionCombinationViewSettings::SetStandardCombination

### What should Tapir let you do?

Follow-up of #846: #847 added rename/delete, but reading and setting which design option combination a saved view shows was left out (no way to get an `ACAPI::ModelViews::View` from a navigator item). The bot suggested a new issue for just this part. The missing piece is in the public DevKit docs: `ACAPI::ModelViews::FindViewByGuid (const API_Guid&)`, "compatible with the guid member of API_NavigatorItem" (BenTristem quoted it in #846).

**Our case** (Archicad 29 AUT, Tapir 1.7.1): 4 walls and a slab on a roof were missing from all plans. We first blamed a renovation filter (the project has none). They are linked to the design option "Hiden :: Pool", which no combination activates. `FilterElements` on these 5 elements, same result on a layout and on their own floor plan:

| filter | passes |
|---|---|
| `IsVisibleByRenovation` | 0 / 5 |
| `IsOverriddenByRenovation` | 5 / 5 |
| `IsVisibleByLayer` | 5 / 5 |
| `IsVisibleIn3D` | 0 / 5 |

`GetDesignOptionForElements` shows the link ("LinkedToDesignOption", "Pool"), but nothing tells which combination a view shows, so a script cannot say "hidden by the design option combination of this view".

**Proposed**
1. `GetDesignOptionCombinationOfViews {"navigatorItemIds": [...]}` → per view `{"status": "MainModelOnly" | "Standard" | "Custom" | "Missing", "name": "…", "designOptionCombinationId": {...} (for Standard)}`.
2. `SetDesignOptionCombinationOfViews {"navigatorItemIdsWithCombination": [{"navigatorItemId", "designOptionCombinationId" | "mainModelOnly": true}]}`.
3. In the `FilterElements` schema, a note that elements hidden by design options fail `IsVisibleByRenovation` and pass `IsOverriddenByRenovation` (as measured above), so nobody reads it as a renovation filter.

### Declarations from the DevKit (optional)

```cpp
// From the public DevKit docs (Archicad 30 C++ API pages)

// ACAPI::DesignOptions::DesignOptionManager
Result<DesignOptionCombinationViewSettings> GetDesignOptionCombinationSettingsOf (const ACAPI::ModelViews::View& view) const;

// ACAPI::DesignOptions::DesignOptionCombinationViewSettings (DesignOptionCombinationViewSettings.hpp)
// "the design option combination settings of a view"
