### What should Tapir let you do?

Expose the remaining open Structural Analytical Model functions (groups Analytical / AnalyticalModel on the [API coverage checklist](https://enzyme-apd.github.io/tapir-archicad-automation/api-coverage/)) through Tapir JSON commands, in a new **Analytical** command group: a new option of an existing command where one fits, otherwise a new command. Their parameters become the command's input and their results the response. GUIDs (analytical model, elements, load groups/cases/combinations) go in and out as Tapir's usual GUID objects; the `API_Token` every function takes is the add-on's own, not a command input.

Suggested command split (one PR per part):
1. **Analytical model** — get the current / per-variation analytical model, its model variation, update it, visibility settings (get/set), generation settings to no rule, model check type id, complementary project member type.
2. **Members** — curve/surface members and the elements that have them (`GetCurveElements`, `GetSurfaceElements`, `GetCurveMember`, `GetSurfaceMember`, `GetSegmentedSurfaceMember`), member connections, part-ref coord/curve, LCS of members, releases (get/set), custom curve member stretch values (AC29+), create element from surface member.
3. **Load groups / cases / combinations** — list and get them, delete them (creating and adding are already tracked in #1192, #1194–#1196).
4. **Supports and links** — geometry, get-from-element / set-element-from.
5. **Point, edge and surface loads** — geometry (incl. the AC25-only `ACAPI_AnalyticalModel_*` geometry getters), get-from-element / set-element-from, edge/surface load custom data to and from memo.

Related, already filed separately: #1192, #1193, #1194, #1195, #1196, #1197, #1198 (#1199 and #1200 are duplicates of #1198).

