This takes over #1220, #1249, #1219 and #1265. Each stopped because the bot had no DevKit: it asked for the include paths, the namespaces and the declarations of `ACAPI::Library::GSMObject`, `Library` and `LibraryManager`, and how to turn a `GS::UnID` into a string. All of that is below, from the AC28–AC30 DevKits the build checks use (28.3001, 29.3000, 30.3000). As the requester I've made the design decisions the bot asked for.

**For every part:**
- **Includes and namespace:** `LibraryCommands.cpp` on `main` already includes `ACAPI/Library/LibraryManager.hpp` and `ACAPI/Library/GSMObject.hpp` under `#ifdef ServerMainVers_2800`, uses `ACAPI::Library::GSMObject` and calls `ACAPI::Library::GetLibraryManager ()` and `GetGSMObjectOfLibPart`. Build on that. AC28 declares the classes in `ACAPI::Library::v1` followed by `using namespace v1;`, so `ACAPI::Library::GSMObject` names them on AC28, AC29 and AC30 alike. Everything is AC28+; older versions return "requires Archicad 28 or newer".
- **Identity:** `GS::UnID::ToUniString ()` (in `GSUtils/GSUnID.hpp`) gives the string form; `GetMainGuid ()` / `GetRevGuid ()` the GUIDs, as `ElementCommands.cpp` already reads them. Return `unID` as that string.
- **Results:** handle `ACAPI::Result` with `IsOk` / `Unwrap` / `UnwrapErr`, as `LibraryCommands.cpp` does. Each item gets its own error.
- **Library part input:** `libraryPartName` (the file name with extension, `GetLibPartByName`) or `element` (its `libInd`, `GetLibPartByLibInd`), as #1220's thread settled.

## 1. Read the scripts of a library part (#1220)

`GetLibraryPartScripts {libraryParts: [...], scripts?: ["master", "parameter", "2d", "3d", "properties"], password?}`. It uses the same keys as `SetLibraryPartScripts`' table on `main`. For each requested script it returns `{present, script}`: `present` comes from `Has…Script`, `script` from `Get…Script (password)` and is left out when the script is not present. A wrong password or a part that is not a GSM object is an error for that item.

## 2. Package information of libraries (#1249)

`GetLibraries` gets an optional `package` object for each library. Find the library with `GetLibraryManager ()->FindLibraries` and match it to `API_LibraryInfo.location` through `GetLocation ()` with the existing `SameLocation`. The object holds `{packageId, mainVersion, subVersion, minArchicadVersion, minArchicadBuildNumber, dependencies: [{name, packageId, version}]}`, from `GetPackageID`, `GetPackageMainVersion`, `GetPackageSubVersion`, `GetPackageMinACVersion`, `GetPackageMinACBuildNumber` and `GetPackageDependencies`. The dependency tuple is name, GUID, version. Leave `package` out when `IsPackage ()` is false or fails.

## 3. Copy a library part under a new name (#1219)

`CopyLibraryParts {libraryParts: [{libraryPartName | element, newName, targetFolder?, keepMainGuid?}]}`:
- `targetFolder` defaults to the embedded library (`GetEmbeddedLibrary ()`, then `GetLocation ()`).
- `keepMainGuid` defaults to false, which means `CopyMethod::GenerateNewUnID`; true means `KeepMainGuid`.
- It refuses when `targetFolder/newName` already exists.
- After `CopyTo` it loads the copy with `LoadGSMObjectFromFile` and returns its `unID` (`GetUnID`) and `path`.
- Then it calls `ACAPI_ProjectOperation_ReloadLibraries ()` once for the whole call, as `ReloadLibraries` does, so the copy can be found by name.

## 4. Read a .gsm file without loading it (#1265)

`GetLibraryPartFileInfo {files: [path]}`: `LoadGSMObjectFromFile`, then `unID`, `subTypeUnID` (`GetSubTypeUnID`) and the scripts as in part 1. The part is not registered in the project. Parameters are left out of this issue: `GetParameters` returns `GDL::Parameters`, which nothing on `main` reads yet. They follow once `SetLibraryPartParameters` (#1468) has settled how `GDL::Parameters` maps to JSON.

