## 2. Drawing primitives of elements and of the story control (#1069, #1070)

- `GetDrawingPrimitivesOfElements {elements}` (AC27+, `ACAPI_DrawingPrimitive_ShapePrims`): returns `primitives` for each element, as one generic list. Each item is `{type, …}`, where `type` is the `API_PrimTypeID` name without its prefix (`Point`, `Line`, `Arc`, `Text`, `PLine`, `Tri`, `Poly`, `Pict`, `Ctrl`, `Hotspot`, …). The other keys are that struct's fields: `API_Prim_Head` as `pen`, `layer`, `drwIndex`, `inEdit`, … and the geometry as coordinates. For `Poly`, `Tri` and `PLine` the coordinates come from the callback's parameters, as `CollectCutFillPolygons` reads them on `main` (`ElementCommands.cpp`). `Pict` returns only its bounding box and the `Text` string. `Ctrl` items stay in the list, so sub-parts can be recognised. The callback has no user pointer, so collect into a file-static collector, as `CollectCutFillPolygons` does. The floor plan must be the current database; otherwise return an error that says so.
- `GetStoryControlPrimitives {databaseId}` (AC25+, `ACAPI_DrawingPrimitive_DrawStoryControl`): the same primitive list for the story levels drawn in a section, elevation or interior elevation database. `databaseId` is what `GetDatabaseIdFromNavigatorItemId` returns.

