## 3. Library part pictures from base64 PNG (left out of #1469)

`SetLibraryPartPictureImages {name, previewPicture?, gdlPictures?, darkPreviewPicture?, darkGdlPictures?}` (AC28+; the dark ones need AC29+). It's a new command, so #1469's `SetLibraryPartPictures` stays untouched. Each picture is a base64 PNG, decoded in three steps:
1. `Base64Converter::Decode (const GS::UniString&)`, which returns a `GS::Array<char>` (`GSXMLUtils/Base64Converter.hpp`, a namespace; `main` already includes it for `Encode`);
2. `NewDisplay::NativeImage (const char* data, UInt32 size, NewDisplay::NativeImage::Encoding::PNG)` (`Graphix/NativeImage.hpp`; the `Encoding` enum is `JPEG = 0, PNG = 1, Unknown`, and the constructor is the same in AC28–AC30);
3. `GX::Image (const NewDisplay::NativeImage&)` (`GXImage/GXImage.hpp`), passed as `GX::ImageRef` to the setter.

An image that decodes empty, with width 0, is that picture's error. All setters run in one `Modify`.

- `ACAPI::Library::GSMObject::Modifier::SetPreviewPicture` (AC28–30, `GSMObject.hpp`): `ACAPI::Result<void> SetPreviewPicture (const GX::ImageRef& image)`
- `ACAPI::Library::GSMObject::Modifier::SetGDLPictures` (AC28–30, `GSMObject.hpp`): `ACAPI::Result<void> SetGDLPictures (const std::vector<GX::ImageRef>& images)`
- `ACAPI::Library::GSMObject::Modifier::SetDarkPreviewPicture` (AC29–30, `GSMObject.hpp`): `ACAPI::Result<void> SetDarkPreviewPicture (const GX::ImageRef& image)`
- `ACAPI::Library::GSMObject::Modifier::SetDarkGDLPictures` (AC29–30, `GSMObject.hpp`): `ACAPI::Result<void> SetDarkGDLPictures (const std::vector<GX::ImageRef>& images)`

