## 3. MEP defaults used for placing (AC27+)

A default object is an in-memory set of settings used to place new elements. The DevKit can't write one back as the tool's settings (that's why #1522 dropped `ModifyMEPToolDefaults`), so these only change what gets placed.
- `GetMEPToolDefaults {elementType, domain?}`: reads the tool default (`main` already gets it for placing) and returns its settings: routing node and segment defaults, rigid segment `width`/`height`/`shape` (AC27–28 getters; AC29+ as `main` reads them), port defaults (AC30, `Get…PortDefaults`; AC27 `GetShapeOfPort`), insulation, and `circuitDefaultCount` for electrical panels (AC30).
- `CreateMEPRoutingElements` and `CreateMEPElements` (on `main`): add an optional `defaults` object. Without `fromScratch` the command starts from the tool default as now; with `fromScratch: true` from a fresh `Create…Default (domain)`. It applies the given keys through the default's modifiers (`SetRoutingNodeDefault`, `SetBendDefault` AC27–28 / `SetElbowDefault` AC29+, `SetTransitionDefault`, `SetRigidSegmentDefault`, elbow `SetFactorRadius`, `SetPreferenceTable` of elbows and transitions, `SetInsulationThickness` / `RemoveInsulation`) and then places as now.
- `CreateMEPFlexibleSegments {segments: [{polyline, startDirection?, endDirection?, domain}]}` (AC28+): `FlexibleSegmentDefault::PlacePolyline`, returning the new ids.
- `ModifyElectricalProjectSettings` (on `main`, AC30): add `clearLoadClassifications` and `clearWiringTypes` booleans, applied before any given lists.

